(with default `XXH_ACCEPT_NULL_INPUT_POINTER == 0`) (`xxhash.c:454-458`) | `XXH_ERROR` = `1` |\n| 141 | `XXH64_update` / `XXH64_update_endian` | `input == NULL` (default config) (`xxhash.c:914-918`) | `XXH_ERROR` = `1` |\n| 142 | `XXH32_createState` | `XXH_malloc` fails (`xxhash.c:422-424`) | `NULL` |\n| 143 | `XXH64_createState` | `XXH_malloc` fails (`xxhash.c:884-886`) | `NULL` |\n\n### Notes\n\n- **Clamps, not rejections** (invalid input is silently coerced, never an error): `acceleration < 1 → LZ4_ACCELERATION_DEFAULT(1)` and `> LZ4_ACCELERATION_MAX(65537) → 65537` in `LZ4_compress_fast_extState` (`lz4.c:1386-1387`), `_fastReset` (`lz4.c:1417-1418`), `LZ4_compress_fast_continue` (`lz4.c:1719-1720`); `LZ4_setCompressionLevel`: `<1 → LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT(9)`, `>LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX(12) → 12` (`lz4hc.c:1614-1615`); `LZ4HC_getCLevelParams`: same clamp (`lz4hc.c:112-114`); `LZ4_saveDict` clamps `dictSize` to 64 KB and to `dict->dictSize` (`lz4.c:1820-1821`); `LZ4_saveDictHC` clamps to 64 KB, forces `<4 → 0`, clamps to `prefixSize` (`lz4hc.c:1748-1750`); `LZ4_loadDictHC` truncates `dictSize > 64 KB` to the last 64 KB (`lz4hc.c:1634-1637`); `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` truncates dict to last 64 KB (`lz4frame.c:546-549`); `LZ4F_getBlockSize` remaps `blockSizeID == 0` to `LZ4F_BLOCKSIZEID_DEFAULT` before range-checking (`lz4frame.c:337`); `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` silently does `dstCapacity = MIN(targetOutputSize, dstCapacity)`.\n- **Never-raised error codes.** Exhaustive grep shows these `LZ4F_errorCodes` variants exist in the enum/string table but have **no** raise site anywhere in `lz4.c`, `lz4hc.c`, `lz4frame.c`, `lz4file.c`: `LZ4F_ERROR_GENERIC`, `LZ4F_ERROR_blockMode_invalid`, `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid`, `LZ4F_ERROR_srcSize_tooLarge`. A port need not be able to produce codes 1, 3, 5, 10.\n- **Compile-time-only guards** (no runtime branch): `#error` if `LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE < LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE_MIN (10)` or `> LZ4_MEMORY_USAGE_MAX (20)` (`lz4.h:166-172`, default 14); `LZ4F_STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(ptrdiff_t) >= sizeof(size_t))` in `LZ4F_returnErrorCode` (`lz4frame.c:314`); `XXH_STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(XXH32_canonical_t) == sizeof(XXH32_hash_t))` (`xxhash.c:567`, `1020`).\n- **`FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION`** disables rows 97, 103, 112, 113, 117 (magic number, header checksum, block checksum ×2, content checksum). Default builds enable all.\n- **Asserts are not rejections.** ~120 `assert()` calls exist; all compile to `((void)0)` unless `assert(0)`-style debug builds (`lz4.c:273`, `lz4frame.c:147`). Notable \"impossible case\" asserts: `lz4.c:813`, `826`, `866`; `xxhash.c:346`, `806`. They must **not** be translated into runtime errors.\n\n### `LZ4F_errorCodes` enum values (declaration order, from `LZ4F_LIST_ERRORS` at `lz4frame.h:653-678`)\n\n| index | name | `(size_t)-code` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | `LZ4F_OK_NoError` | `0` (not an error) |\n| 1 | `LZ4F_ERROR_GENERIC` | `(size_t)-1` |\n| 2 | `LZ4F_ERROR_maxBlockSize_invalid` | `(size_t)-2` |\n| 3 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockMode_invalid` | `(size_t)-3` |\n| 4 | `LZ4F_ERROR_parameter_invalid` | `(size_t)-4` |\n| 5 | `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid` | `(size_t)-5` |\n| 6 | `LZ4F_ERROR_headerVersion_wrong` | `(size_t)-6` |\n| 7 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockChecksum_invalid` | `(size_t)-7` |\n| 8 | `LZ4F_ERROR_reservedFlag_set` | `(size_t)-8` |\n| 9 | `LZ4F_ERROR_allocation_failed` | `(size_t)-9` |\n| 10 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcSize_tooLarge` | `(size_t)-10` |\n| 11 | `LZ4F_ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall` | `(size_t)-11` |\n| 12 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameHeader_incomplete` | `(size_t)-12` |\n| 13 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameType_unknown` | `(size_t)-13` |\n| 14 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameSize_wrong` | `(size_t)-14` |\n| 15 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcPtr_wrong` | `(size_t)-15` |\n| 16 | `LZ4F_ERROR_decompressionFailed` | `(size_t)-16` |\n| 17 | `LZ4F_ERROR_headerChecksum_invalid` | `(size_t)-17` |\n| 18 | `LZ4F_ERROR_contentChecksum_invalid` | `(size_t)-18` |\n| 19 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameDecoding_alreadyStarted` | `(size_t)-19` |\n| 20 |