y)`). `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k` / `LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k` (these read 64KB BEFORE dst — allocate a buffer with 64KB of slack before the output region and pass `buf.as_mut_ptr().add(65536)`, and make sure the prefix content is IDENTICAL in the C and Rust runs).\n\nF. Dictionary / streaming compression. Exercise all three dictionary regimes:\n   - prefix (contiguous: compress consecutive chunks of one buffer with `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`)\n   - extDict (separate dict buffer via `LZ4_loadDict`, then compress from a different buffer)\n   - dictCtx (`LZ4_attach_dictionary` against a separate loaded stream)\n   For each: `LZ4_createStream` + `LZ4_resetStream` / `LZ4_resetStream_fast` / `LZ4_initStream` on an `Aligned` buffer; `LZ4_loadDict` vs `LZ4_loadDictSlow` vs `LZ4_loadDict_internal` (its 4th arg is `LoadDict_mode_e`: 0 == `_ld_fast`, 1 == `_ld_slow` — verify against `c_src/src/lz4.c`); dict sizes 0, 1, 4, 7, 8 (HASH_UNIT), 9, 100, 65535, 65536, 65537, 100000 (>64KB is truncated to the last 64KB); then N chunks (N in 1..=8) of varying sizes; `LZ4_saveDict` after each round with sizes 0, 1, 4, 100, 65536, 100000; `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict`. Assert the compressed bytes AND the `LZ4_stream_t` state bytes (size `LZ4_sizeofState()`) match between C and Rust after EVERY step, and that every produced stream decompresses correctly.\n\nG. Streaming decompression: `LZ4_createStreamDecode`, `LZ4_setStreamDecode` (with dict / without / NULL dict), `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_continue`, in both a linear-buffer and a RING-BUFFER layout sized by `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize)`. Also the stateless `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict` — with dict == NULL/0, dict adjacent to dst (prefix mode), and dict in a separate buffer (extDict mode).\n\nH. Deprecated/legacy family — call e