exact signatures — do not guess.\n- `translation/tests/xxh.rs` — a working example of the style to follow.\n\nNOTE a harness gotcha: `gen(&mut rng, rng.below(N), shape)` does NOT compile (double mutable borrow). Write `let n = rng.below(N); gen(&mut rng, n, shape);`.\n\nBuild/run commands (ALWAYS use --offline, network is blocked; always add a timeout):\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kMGhHl/translation\ntimeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test block 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nThe C .so already exists at `c_src/build/liblz4.so`; the harness finds both .so files automatically.\n\nGOAL: exhaustive differential tests for the **`lz4.c` block API** (from `c_src/include/lz4.h`). For every configuration, call BOTH libraries via their exports and assert the results are IDENTICAL: return codes AND output bytes byte-for-byte. Use MANY randomized inputs per configuration with FIXED seeds (reproducible), not one hand-picked value.\n\nCover these entry points and configurations (read `c_src/src/lz4.c` and `c_src/include/lz4.h` for exact semantics; the C is always right):\n\nA. Bounds/constants: `LZ4_compressBound` over a large sweep of `int` values including 0, 1, 65535, 65536, 0x7E000000 (LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE), 0x7E000001, INT_MAX, -1, INT_MIN. `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` over the same kind of sweep. `LZ4_sizeofState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState`, `LZ4_versionNumber`, `LZ4_versionString`.\n\nB. One-shot compression, ALL shapes x MANY sizes. Sizes MUST include the thresholds the C branches on: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (MINMATCH), 5 (LASTLITERALS), 11, 12 (MFLIMIT), 13, 15, 16, 63, 64, 65, 254, 255, 256, 511, 512, 513, 4095, 4096, 65534, 65535, 65536, 65537 (LZ4_64Klimit = 64KB+1 selects byU16 vs byU32 tableType), 65538, 131072, 200000, 300000. Entry points: `LZ4_compress_default`, `LZ4_compress_fast` with acceleration in {INT_MIN, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 5, 17, 100, 1000, 65536, 65537, 65538, INT_MAX} (note C CLAMPS out-of-range acceleration — assert both clamp identically), and `LZ4_compress_fast_extState` / `LZ4_compress_fast_extState_fastReset` using an `Aligned` buffer of `LZ4_sizeofState()` bytes with alignment 8. For extState, ALSO assert the resulting state bytes are identical between C and Rust after the call (the state is a public-size struct).\n\nC. dstCapacity sweep — this is where the limitedOutput rejection branches live (ERRORS.md rows 5,6,7). For each input, call with dstCapacity = compressBound, exact compressed size, compressed size - 1, compressed size/2, srcSize, srcSize/2, 1, 0. Assert identical return (0 on failure) and identical bytes in the region actually written.\n\nD. `LZ4_compress_destSize` and `LZ4_compress_destSize_extState`: sweep targetDstSize over many values (0, 1, 2, 5, 12, 16, 64, 300, and fractions of compressBound). BOTH the returned int AND the in/out `*srcSizePtr` value must match. Then verify the produced block decompresses to exactly the consumed prefix.\n\nE. Decompression: `LZ4_decompress_safe` on valid blocks (all of the above) with dstCapacity = exact, exact+1, exact-1, 0. `LZ4_decompress_fast` with the exact originalSize. `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial` with targetOutputSize sweeping 0..=srcSize (many values) and dstCapacity both >= and < targetOutputSize (the C clamps `dstCapacity = MIN(target, dstCapacity)`). `LZ4_decompress_safe_withPrefix64k` / `LZ4_decompress_fast_withPrefix64k` (these read 64KB BEFORE dst — allocate a buffer with 64KB of slack before the output region and pass `buf.as_mut_ptr().add(65536)`, and make sure the prefix content is IDENTICAL in the C and Rust runs).\n\nF. Dictionary / streaming compression. Exercise all three dictionary regimes:\n   - prefix (contiguous: compress consecutive chunks of one buffer with `LZ4_compress_fast_continue`)\n   - extDict (separate dict buffer via `LZ4_loadDict`, then compress from a different buffer)\n   - dictCtx (`LZ4_attach_dictionary` against a separate loaded stream)\n   For each: `LZ4_createStream` + `LZ4_resetStream` / `LZ4_resetStream_fast` / `LZ4_initStream` on an `Aligned` buffer; `LZ4_loadDict` vs `LZ4_loadDictSlow` vs `LZ4_loadDict_internal` (its 4th arg is `LoadDict_mode_e`: 0 == `_ld_fast`, 1 == `_ld_slow` — verify against `c_src/src/lz4.c`); dict sizes 0, 1, 4, 7, 8 (HASH_UNIT), 9, 100, 65535, 65536, 65537, 100000 (>64KB is truncated to the last 64KB); then N chunks (N in 1..=8) of varying sizes; `LZ4_saveDict` after each round with sizes 0, 1, 4, 100, 65536, 100000; `LZ4_compress_forceExtDict`. Assert the compressed bytes AND the `LZ4_stream_t` state bytes (size `LZ4_sizeofState()`) match between C and Rust after EVERY step, and that every produced stream decompresses correctly.\n\nG. Streaming decompression: `LZ4_createStreamDecode`, `LZ4_setStreamDecode` (with dict / without / NULL dict), `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_continue`, in both a linear-buffer and a RING-BUFFER layout sized by `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize(maxBlockSize)`. Also the stateless `LZ4_decompress_safe_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_fast_usingDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_forceExtDict`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial_forceExtDict` — with dict == NULL/0, dict adjacent to dst (prefix mode), and dict in a separate buffer (extDict mode).\n\nH. Deprecated/legacy family — call each at least once with several inputs and assert identical results: `LZ4_compress`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput`, `LZ4_compress_withState`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_withState`, `LZ4_compress_continue`, `LZ4_compress_limitedOutput_continue`, `LZ4_uncompress`, `LZ4_uncompress_unknownOutputSize`, `LZ4_create` (allocates from a caller `char*` buffer of `LZ4_sizeofStreamState()` bytes), `LZ4_slideInputBuffer`, `LZ4_resetStreamState`, `LZ4_sizeofStreamState`.\n\nI. Error paths (must return the SAME sentinel, not merely \"both failed\"):\n   - `LZ4_compressBound` with oversized/negative -> 0\n   - compression with srcSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE or negative srcSize -> 0. (Do NOT actually allocate 2GB: pass a small real buffer but a huge/negative srcSize value; the C returns 0 from the range check BEFORE touching memory. Verify by reading lz4.c:1360 that the check precedes any access.)\n   - `LZ4_initStream(NULL, n)`, `LZ4_initStream(buf, size-1)`, `LZ4_initStream(misaligned_ptr, size)` -> all NULL\n   - `LZ4_freeStream(NULL)`, `LZ4_freeStreamDecode(NULL)` -> 0\n   - `LZ4_loadDict(stream, NULL, n)`, `LZ4_loadDict(stream, dict, 0)`, dictSize < 8\n   - `LZ4_decompress_safe(NULL, dst, n, m)` -> -1; `outputSize < 0` -> -1; `srcSize == 0 && outputSize > 0` -> -1; `outputSize == 0` with srcSize==1 and src[0]==0 -> 0, but any other srcSize/content -> -1\n   - CORRUPT/TRUNCATED input fuzzing: take a valid compressed block, then (i) truncate it at every length, (ii) flip single bits / bytes at many random positions, (iii) feed purely random bytes as \"compressed\" data. For EVERY such input assert the EXACT int returned by C == the EXACT int returned by Rust (the `_output_error` value encodes how far into the input the error was found, so exact equality matters). Do this for `LZ4_decompress_safe`, `LZ4_decompress_fast`, `LZ4_decompress_safe_partial`, and the `usingDict` variants. Use a fixed seed and a few thousand iterations — this is the highest-value test in the file.\n\nKeep every test's runtime modest (the whole file should run in well under 300 seconds). Add `#[test]` functions with descriptive names, `mod common; use common::*;` at the top, and doc comments citing the ERRORS.md/CONFIGS.md concern each covers.\n\nDELIVERABLE: `translation/tests/block.rs` compiles cleanly and you have RUN it. Report:\n1. the exact `cargo test` summary line,\n2. a list of every test that FAILS, and for each the precise divergence (inputs, C value, Rust value) — do not fix it,\n3. the number of `#[test]` functions you wrote.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-p6FJeW/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-kMGhHl/efa97b54-4a20-