{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019KW6CJBEoqwuiwFXXKBz9V","type":"tool_result","content":"# ERRORS.md — Error-surface table\n\nDerived mechanically from the C sources (`c_src/src/{lz4,lz4hc,lz4frame,lz4file,xxhash}.c`,\n`c_src/include/*.h`) by grepping every `RETURN_ERROR`, `return -1`, `return 0`, `return NULL`,\n`_output_error`, `err0r`, `rvl_error`, `XXH_ERROR`, `assert`, explicit range check, null check\nand min/max constant.\n\n## Conventions\n\n* `LZ4F_*` functions return errors as `(size_t)-(ptrdiff_t)code`.\n  `LZ4F_isError(r)` is `r > (size_t)(-LZ4F_ERROR_maxCode)` = `r > SIZE_MAX-24`,\n  so exactly codes **1..23** are detectable errors.\n* `_output_error` in `LZ4_decompress_generic` expands to\n  `return (int)(-(ip - (const BYTE*)src)) - 1` — a *negative* value whose exact\n  magnitude depends on how far into the input the error was detected. Tests must\n  compare the exact int returned by C vs Rust, not merely \"both < 0\".\n* `rvl_error` is `(Rvl_t)(-1)`, an internal sentinel, surfaced through `_output_error`.\n* `XXH_ERROR` = `1`, `XXH_OK` = `0`.\n\n## `LZ4F_errorCodes` values (declaration order = numeric value)\n\n| code | name | returned value |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | `LZ4F_OK_NoError` | `0` (not an error) |\n| 1 | `LZ4F_ERROR_GENERIC` | `(size_t)-1` |\n| 2 | `LZ4F_ERROR_maxBlockSize_invalid` | `(size_t)-2` |\n| 3 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockMode_invalid` | `(size_t)-3` |\n| 4 | `LZ4F_ERROR_parameter_invalid` | `(size_t)-4` |\n| 5 | `LZ4F_ERROR_compressionLevel_invalid` | `(size_t)-5` |\n| 6 | `LZ4F_ERROR_headerVersion_wrong` | `(size_t)-6` |\n| 7 | `LZ4F_ERROR_blockChecksum_invalid` | `(size_t)-7` |\n| 8 | `LZ4F_ERROR_reservedFlag_set` | `(size_t)-8` |\n| 9 | `LZ4F_ERROR_allocation_failed` | `(size_t)-9` |\n| 10 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcSize_tooLarge` | `(size_t)-10` |\n| 11 | `LZ4F_ERROR_dstMaxSize_tooSmall` | `(size_t)-11` |\n| 12 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameHeader_incomplete` | `(size_t)-12` |\n| 13 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameType_unknown` | `(size_t)-13` |\n| 14 | `LZ4F_ERROR_frameSize_wrong` | `(size_t)-14` |\n| 15 | `LZ4F_ERROR_srcPtr_wrong` | `(size_t)-15` |\n| 16 | `LZ4F_ERROR_decompressionFailed` | `(size_t)-16` |\n...\n103:| 45 | `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` | `maxBlockSize < 0` (`lz4.c:2617`) | `0` | [ ] |\n104:| 46 | `LZ4_decoderRingBufferSize` | `maxBlockSize > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (`lz4.c:2618`) | `0` | [ ] |\n105:| 47 | `LZ4_decompress_safe_continue` / `_fast_continue` | inner decode returns `<= 0` → forwarded, stream state NOT advanced (`lz4.c:2681`,`2688`,`2694`,`2696`,`2700`,`2705`) | forwarded value | [ ] |\n106:| 48 | `LZ4_setStreamDecode` | `dictionary == NULL`/`dictSize == 0` reset form vs invalid | `1` (always succeeds) | [ ] |\n107:| 49 | `LZ4_compress_HC` (`LZ4HC_encodeSequence`, limited) | literals do not fit: `op+(length/255)+length+(2+1+LASTLITERALS) > oend` (`lz4hc.c:308`) | `1` internally → caller `0` | [ ] |\n108:| 50 | `LZ4_compress_HC` (`LZ4HC_encodeSequence`, limited) | match encoding does not fit output (`lz4hc.c:333`) | `1` internally → caller `0` | [ ] |\n109:| 51 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 1..2 (`LZ4MID_compress`) | `*srcSizePtr < 0` (`lz4hc.c:559`) | `0` | [ ] |\n110:| 52 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 1..2 | `maxOutputSize < 0` (`lz4hc.c:560`) | `0` | [ ] |\n111:| 53 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 1..2 | `*srcSizePtr > LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (`lz4hc.c:563`) | `0` | [ ] |\n112:| 54 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 1..2 | limitedOutput and last literal run does not fit (`lz4hc.c:714`) | `0` | [ ] |\n113:| 55 | `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` clevel 1..2 | `_lz4mid_dest_overflow` — fillOutput exhausted (`lz4hc.c:772`) | `0` | [ ] |\n114:| 56 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 3..9 (`hashChain`) | limitedOutput and last literal run does not fit (`lz4hc.c:1315`) | `0` | [ ] |\n115:| 57 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 3..9 | `_dest_overflow` — compression failed (`lz4hc.c:1361`) | `0` | [ ] |\n116:| 58 | `LZ4_compress_HC` clevel 10..12 (`optimal`) | limitedOutput and last literal run does not fit → `retval = 0` (`lz4hc.c:2066`) | `0` | [ ] |\n117:| 59 | `LZ4HC_compress_generic_internal` | `limit == fillOutput && dstCapacity < 1` (`lz4hc.c:1388`) | `0` | [ ] |\n118:| 60 | `LZ4HC_compress_generic_internal` | `(U32)*srcSizePtr > (U32)LZ4_MAX_INPUT_SIZE` (too large or negative) (`lz4hc.c:1389`) | `0` | [ ] |\n119:| 61 | `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset` | `state` misaligned vs `LZ4_streamHC_t_alignment()` (`lz4hc.c:1503`) | `0` | [ ] |\n120:| 62 | `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC` | `LZ4_initStreamHC(state,size)` returns NULL (NULL / undersized / misaligned) (`lz4hc.c:1515`) | `0` | [ ] |\n121:| 63 | `LZ4_compress_HC_destSize` | `LZ4_initStreamHC` returns NULL (`lz4hc.c:1541`) | `0` | [ ] |\n122:| 64 | `LZ4_createStreamHC` / `LZ4_createHC` | `ALLOC_AND_ZERO` failure (`lz4hc.c:1558`, `2162`) — not FFI-triggerable | `NULL` | [ ] |\n123:| 65 | `LZ4_freeStreamHC` | `LZ4_streamHCPtr == NULL` (`lz4hc.c:1566`) | `0` | [ ] |\n124:| 66 | `LZ4_initStreamHC` | `buffer == NULL` (`lz4hc.c:1578`) | `NULL` | [ ] |\n125:| 67 | `LZ4_initStreamHC` | `size < sizeof(LZ4_streamHC_t)` (`lz4hc.c:1579`) | `NULL` | [ ] |\n126:| 68 | `LZ4_initStreamHC` | `buffer` misaligned (`lz4hc.c:1580`) | `NULL` | [ ] |\n127:| 69 | `LZ4_resetStreamStateHC` | `LZ4_initStreamHC` returns NULL (NULL/misaligned state) (`lz4hc.c:2153`) | `1` (nonzero == error) | [ ] |\n128:| 70 | `LZ4_freeHC` | `LZ4HC_Data == NULL` (`lz4hc.c:2169`) | `0` | [ ] |\n129:| 71 | `LZ4F_getBlockSize` | `blockSizeID < 4` after 0→default remap, or `> 7` (`lz4frame.c:337-339`) | `(size_t)-2` `maxBlockSize_invalid` | [ ] |\n130:| 72 | `LZ4F_getBlockSize` | out-of-range enum value across FFI (e.g. 8, 99, -1, INT_MAX) | `(size_t)-2` | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018bt2yhfDZosfXEkX2jb3me","session_id":"efa97b54-4a20-4ac7-b60b-5dc425f1ad2b","uuid":"553d437f-32cf-4821-aa89-cfc7e0573979","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:48:05.772Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write HC API diff tests"}
