pressFrame_usingCDict` requires a **non-NULL cctx** (it is dereferenced by `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict`). Only `LZ4F_compressFrame` allocates one for you.\n- `LZ4F_createCDict(ptr, dictSize)` unconditionally `memcpy`s `dictSize` bytes, so never pass NULL with a non-zero size.\n- An out-of-range `blockSizeID` can make `LZ4F_compressBound` return gigabytes — never allocate from an unvalidated bound.\n\nBuild/run (ALWAYS `--offline`; always use a timeout; other agents may hold the cargo lock, so retry once if it blocks):\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kMGhHl/translation\ntimeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test frame 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test |^error|test result|panicked|SIGSEGV\" | head -40\n```\n\nGOAL: for EVERY valid configuration below, drive BOTH libraries through their `.so` exports and assert the results are IDENTICAL: every return code, every in/out `*srcSizePtr` / `*dstSizePtr`, and the produced bytes byte-for-byte. Use MANY randomized inputs per configuration with FIXED seeds. Read `c_src/src/lz4frame.c` and `c_src/include/lz4frame.h` for exact semantics — the C is always right.\n\nThese are the CONFIGS.md rows you must cover (numbers are for your doc comments):\n\n**89-92 bounds/metadata.** `LZ4F_getVersion`, `LZ4F_compressionLevel_max`, `LZ4F_getBlockSize` (valid IDs), and `LZ4F_compressBound` / `LZ4F_compressFrameBound` over the FULL cross-product of {blockSizeID 0,4,5,6,7} x {blockMode 0,1} x {contentChecksum 0,1} x {blockChecksum 0,1} x {autoFlush 0,1} x {compressionLevel -5,0,1,2,9,12} x {srcSize 0,1,100,65535,65536,65537,262144,1048576,4194304,4194305} and ALSO with `prefsPtr == NULL`.\n\n**93-96 one-shot `LZ4F_compressFrame`.** The same option cross-product x all `Shape`s x the same size list. Include: prefs NULL; `blockSizeID=7` with a tiny srcSize (`LZ4F_optimalBSID` downgrade to 4); `srcSize <= getBlockSize(bsid)` (blockMode force-independent); `srcSize == blockSize+1` with linked; a non-zero declared `contentSize` (auto-corrected to the real srcSize); a non-zero `dictID`; `favorDecSpeed` 0/1 at levels below AND above 10. Verify every frame decompresses back to the original through BOTH libraries.\n\n**97 CDict.** `LZ4F_createCDict` / `LZ4F_createCDict_advanced` / `LZ4F_freeCDict` / `LZ4F_compressFrame_usingCDict` / `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingCDict` with dict sizes 0,1,4,8,64,4096,65535,65536,65537,100000,200000 (>64 KB keeps only the LAST 64 KB) x levels {0,1,2,9,12} x blockMode {linked, independent} (independent re-attaches the cdict per block and takes a DIFFERENT internal path). Also drive `_advanced` with a working `CustomMem` (allocator that succeeds) and confirm the output equals the default-allocator output.\n\n**98-106 streaming compression.** Full `LZ4F_createCompressionContext` -> `LZ4F_compressBegin*` -> N x `LZ4F_compressUpdate` -> `LZ4F_flush` -> `LZ4F_compressEnd` pipelines. Cover:\n   - all four `compressBegin` variants: `LZ4F_compressBegin`, `_usingDict`, `_usingDictOnce`, `_usingCDict`, plus the exported internal `LZ4F_compressBegin_internal` (signature: `cctx, dst, dstCapacity, dictBuffer, dictSize, cdict, prefs`).\n   - header-length combinations: contentSize 0 vs non-zero, dictID 0 vs non-zero -> header sizes 7 / 11 / 15 / 19. Assert `LZ4F_headerSize` on the produced frame agrees between C and Rust and matches the actual bytes emitted.\n   - the tmpBuff sizing matrix: (autoFlush, blockMode) in {(1,linked),(1,independent),(0,linked),(0,independent)} — row 101.\n   - REUSING one cctx for several frames back-to-back, including switching compressionLevel from 9 to 0 between frames (row 99: the buffer is kept but re-initialised as `LZ4_stream_t`) and switching blockSizeID between frames.\n   - update chunk shapes relative to the frame block size: many chunks of 1 byte; chunks of exactly blockSize; blockSize+1; blockSize-1; random chunk sizes; a single giant chunk. Do this for every blockSizeID.\n   - `LZ4F_compressOptions_t.stableSrc` = 0 and 1 with blockMode=linked (row 110 — a genuinely different internal dictionary path).\n   - `LZ4F_flush` interleaved between updates (both when there is buffered data and when there is none -> returns 0).\n   - incompressible input so blocks are STORED with `LZ4F_BLOCKUNCOMPRESSED_FLAG` (row 113), with blockChecksum both off and on.\n   - `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` (row 114): all-stored frames, and ALTERNATING `LZ4F_compressUpdate` / `LZ4F_uncompressedUpdate` on one cctx (the mode change triggers an implicit flush).\n\n**116-137 streaming decompression.** Drive `LZ4F_decompress` / `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` / `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` / `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` / `LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext` (whose return value reports the dStage) over:\n   - input chunking: 1 byte at a time, 4/5/6/7/19/20 bytes, random sizes, and one giant call — for every frame configuration. Header split across calls, block header split across calls, block payload split across calls, block checksum split across calls, content checksum split across calls. Assert the RETURN VALUE (the \"hint\": how many bytes the decoder wants next) matches EXACTLY at every step, along with the bytes consumed/produced.\n   - output chunking: dst buffers of 1, 13, blockSize-1, blockSize, blockSize+1, and huge — this selects between decoding straight into the caller's dst (row 127) and decoding into `tmpOut` + `dstage_flushOut` (row 128).\n   - `LZ4F_decompressOptions_t`: `stableDst` 0/1 (row 133) and `skipChecksums` 0/1 (row 134) — for stableDst=1 you must honour the pledge, i.e. decompress into ONE stable buffer, advancing the pointer, never moving it.\n   - blockMode linked (all the `LZ4F_updateDict` branches, rows 130-132) vs independent (row 136).\n   - SKIPPABLE FRAMES (row 121): build a skippable frame by hand — 4-byte magic in `[LZ4F_MAGIC_SKIPPABLE_START, +15]`, 4-byte little-endian size, then that many arbitrary bytes — and feed it alone, before a real frame, after a real frame, and several in a row, with every input chunk size (1 byte at a time especially, to hit `dstage_storeSFrameSize` and `dstage_skipSkippable`). Cover all 16 skippable magic values and sizes 0, 1, 4, 7, 8, 100, 70000.\n   - CONCATENATED frames: 2-5 valid frames back to back with DIFFERENT preferences each, decoded through one dctx.\n   - `LZ4F_decompress_usingDict` (row 137) with the dict supplied while `dStage <= dstage_init` (honoured) and mid-frame (silently ignored) — build frames that actually USE a dictionary via `LZ4F_compressBegin_usingDict` and confirm the round trip.\n   - `LZ4F_getFrameInfo` on the happy path for every header-length combination; assert every field of the returned `LZ4F_frameInfo_t` matches between C and Rust.\n   - `LZ4F_resetDecompressionContext` mid-frame, then reuse of the same dctx for a fresh frame; and reusing one dctx for many frames without a reset.\n\n**A large randomized end-to-end fuzz** (fixed seed, a few thousand iterations): pick random preferences, a random shape/size, random compress-chunk sizes, random decompress input- and output-chunk sizes, random decompressOptions; run the full compress->decompress pipeline in BOTH libraries; assert every intermediate return code, the compressed bytes, and the recovered plaintext all match, and that the plaintext equals the original.\n\nKeep total runtime under ~400 seconds (use 4 MB block sizes sparingly; prefer many small cases over few huge ones). Add `mod common; use common::*;` at the top and give each `#[test]` a doc comment naming the CONFIGS.md rows it covers.\n\nDELIVERABLE: `translation/tests/frame.rs` compiles cleanly and you have RUN it. Report:\n1. the exact `cargo test` summary line,\n2. every FAILING test with the precise divergence (inputs, C value, Rust value) — do NOT fix the Rust,\n3. the number of `#[test]` functions you wrote,\n4. any CONFIGS row from the list above that you could NOT cover, and why.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-p6FJeW/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-schesch