{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bqb7ugenm5unw4fxhwqowjucvp3xfldywitgkozmrvia24yslana","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The deliverable is complete: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-kMGhHl/translation/tests/hc.rs` (2457 lines, 25 `#[test]` functions), compiled and run.\n\n## 1. compressionLevel thresholds in `c_src/src/lz4hc.c`\n\n`LZ4HC_getCLevelParams()` (lz4hc.c:108-116) is the *only* dispatcher:\n```\nif (cLevel < 1) cLevel = LZ4HC_CLEVEL_DEFAULT (9);\ncLevel = MIN(LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX (12), cLevel);\nreturn k_clTable[cLevel];\n```\n`k_clTable` (lz4hc.c:92-106) → internal compressor selected in `LZ4HC_compress_generic_internal` (lz4hc.c:1396-1411):\n\n| level | strat | compressor | nbSearches / targetLength |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 (unreachable) | `lz4mid` | `LZ4MID_compress` | 2 / 16 |\n| 1 | `lz4mid` | `LZ4MID_compress` | 2 / 16 |\n| 2 (`CLEVEL_MIN`) | `lz4mid` | `LZ4MID_compress` | 2 / 16 |\n| 3–9 | `lz4hc` | `LZ4HC_compress_hashChain` | 4,8,16,32,64,128,256 |\n| 10 (`OPT_MIN`) | `lz4opt` | `LZ4HC_compress_optimal` | 96 / 64 |\n| 11 | `lz4opt` | `LZ4HC_compress_optimal` | 512 / 128 |\n| 12 (`CLEVEL_MAX`) | `lz4opt` | `LZ4HC_compress_optimal` | 16384 / 4096 |\n\nExtra rules found:\n- **There is NO `compressionLevel <= 0` fast-mode fall-through to `LZ4_compress_fast` in this version.** The task brief assumed one; in this lz4hc.c every level `< 1` (incl. `INT_MIN`) is simply remapped to 9 → `hashChain`, 256 searches. I asserted this as an equivalence class instead.\n- `patternAnalysis = (maxNbAttempts > 128)` → only level 9 (and the `<1 → 9` remaps).\n- `fullUpdate` (\"ultra\") in the optimal parser is `cLevel >= LZ4HC_CLEVEL_MAX` using the **raw, unclamped** level, so 12/13/20/100/`INT_MAX` are all identical.\n- `LZ4_setCompressionLevel` (lz4hc.c:1611) clamps the *stored* level with the same `<1 → 9`, `>12 → 12`.\n- `ctx->favorDecSpeed` is only forwarded to `LZ4HC_compress_optimal`, so it cannot change output for effective levels ≤ 9 (asserted).\n- `LZ4_streamHC_t` layout verified by compiling an `offsetof` probe against the real headers: `sizeof == 262200`, `sizeof(LZ4HC_CCtx_internal) == 262192`, alignment 8, `offsetof(dictCtx) == 262184` (used to mask the cross-library pointer field).\n\n## 2. cargo test summary\n```\ntest result: ok. 25 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 15.68s\n```\n(`cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test hc`; 59 s CPU, 18.7 s wall.)\n\n## 3. Failing tests / divergences\n**None.** Every return code, every output byte, every `*srcSizePtr`, every `LZ4_streamHC_t`/extState byte (262200 bytes, all zero-initialised regions included) and every `LZ4HC_match_t {off,len,back}` from `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` matched between C and Rust. `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` proved fully address-independent (3309/13500 randomized calls returned a real match, all identical). Sensitivity was verified: state comparisons run on ~19 000 non-zero bytes, not on empty buffers.\n\nTwo **C-precondition hazards** I had to design around (not Rust bugs, documented in the file):\n- The C `.so` is built **with assertions live** (no `-DNDEBUG`, `-O0`), so any misuse aborts the whole test process. Consequently: `LZ4_loadDictHC` with negative `dictSize` (asserted at lz4hc.c:1632) and \"`LZ4_saveDictHC` on a virgin stream then compress\" (leaves `dictLimit == 0`, trips `assert(matchIndex < ipIndex)`) are excluded.\n- `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC_fastReset(NULL, …)` is *not* an error path: NULL passes `LZ4_isAligned` and is then dereferenced (lz4hc.c:1503-1504) → segfault. Only misaligned states are testable there.\n- Also note `srcSize == 0` must be passed with a *real* allocation: a 0-capacity `Vec`'s dangling `0x1` pointer makes `iend - MFLIMIT` wrap in `LZ4HC_compress_optimal` (lz4hc.c:1846) and the parser dereferences it (I hit this SIGSEGV in both libraries identically and switched to `gen_buf`, which guarantees a heap-backed buffer).\n- \"Undersized state\" for `LZ4_compress_HC_extStateHC` is untestable by construction: the size handed to `LZ4_initStreamHC` is `sizeof(*ctx)`, not user-supplied, so an undersized buffer is a plain overflow rather than a detected error.\n\n## 4. Coverage written\n25 tests: A level sweep small+big sizes (all 20 levels × 8 shapes × 19/6 sizes) + clamping equivalence classes; B extStateHC/_fastReset with state-byte diffing and 120-iteration reuse incl. deliberately failing calls; C destSize + continue_destSize with `*srcSizePtr` and consumed-prefix decode; D capacity sweep (bound/exact/exact-1/half/srcSize/1/0) for 13 level bands via both limitedOutput and fillOutput; E prefix chunks 1..8, extDict with 10 dict sizes, `attach_HC_dictionary` incl. mid-vs-hc `isStateCompatible` failure, `saveDictHC` clamping (`<4→0`, 64 KB, prefixSize) with byte-exact safeBuffer diff, `initStreamHC`/`setCompressionLevel`/`favorDecompressionSpeed`/`resetStreamHC_fast` sequencing; F 13 500 randomized `LZ4HC_searchExtDict` calls; G all 18 deprecated entry points; H rows 49-70 error sentinels; plus two randomized fuzzers (1200 one-shot configs, 700-step streaming state machine)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1077,"cache_read_input_tokens":250204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1077,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018bt2yhfDZosfXEkX2jb3me","session_id":"efa97b54-4a20-4ac7-b60b-5dc425f1ad2b","uuid":"64189985-6974-4eec-95fd-cc478efedcfb","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:11:38.582Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write HC API diff tests"}
