gin_tmpbuff_matrix`, `frame_cctx_reuse_across_frames`, `frame_compressUpdate_chunk_shapes`, `frame_compressUpdate_stableSrc`, `frame_compressUpdate_tmpIn_rewind`, `frame_flush_interleaved`, `frame_stored_blocks_incompressible`, `frame_uncompressedUpdate`, `frame_decompress_input_chunking`, `frame_decompress_output_chunking`, `frame_decompress_options_stableDst_skipChecksums`, `frame_decompress_updateDict_branches`, `frame_decompress_skippable_frames`, `frame_decompress_concatenated_frames`, `frame_decompress_usingDict`, `frame_getFrameInfo_happy_path`, `frame_dctx_reset_and_reuse`, `frame_decompress_dictionary_fuzz`, `frame_end_to_end_fuzz`.\n\nFuzzing: 3000 end-to-end iterations + 600 decoder/dictionary-focused iterations, plus an exhaustive \"split the frame at every offset\" sweep over 4 header/checksum layouts.\n\n## 4. Rows covered with reduced breadth (and why)\n\n- **93-96 (`compressFrame`)** — the full 480-config option cross-product is exercised against **all 8 shapes** for sizes `{0,1,100,65535,65536,65537}` (+`262144` for levels < 2, and `prefsPtr == NULL`). The `{1 MB, 4 MB, 4 MB+1}` sizes are covered for all 8 shapes against a 7-config representative set (`frame_compressFrame_all_shapes_all_sizes`) instead of all 480. The literal product (480 × 8 × 10, including HC level 12 on 4 MB, ×2 libraries) is thousands of seconds of work; a helper `affordable(size, level)` enforces \"no HC above 300 KB\".\n- **Byte-at-a-time chunking** — 1-byte *decompress* feeds run on small frames (≤ 5 KB) and 1-byte *compressUpdate* feeds run on 2 KB inputs for **every** blockSizeID, rather than on multi-megabyte 4 MB-block frames (call-count bound). Larger frames use 4/5/6/7/19/20/random/giant chunks, and the exhaustive split sweep covers every split point of small frames.\n- **Row 129** (`dictSize > 1 GB` truncation) is unreachable from any valid configuration (it needs a >1 GB decoded history) and was not attempted; it was not on the requested list.\n- Error branches inside